The bug was caused by the logic in the `CoordActionInputCheckXCommand` class, which did not properly handle the scenario where a coordinator job had unresolved dependencies, leading to cases where the job did not timeout as expected. The check for whether dependencies were met was incorrectly coupled with the existence of non-existent files, resulting in jobs remaining in a running state instead of timing out when they should have.

