if (isPushDependenciesMet) {
    queue(new CoordActionTimeOutXCommand(coordAction, coordJob.getUser(), coordJob.getAppName()));
} else {
    // Let CoordPushDependencyCheckXCommand queue the timeout
    queue(new CoordPushDependencyCheckXCommand(coordAction.getId()));
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that if push dependencies are met, a timeout command is queued directly, thus handling the unresolved dependencies appropriately. This change ensures that jobs with unresolved dependencies are properly transitioned to a timeout state instead of remaining in a running state indefinitely.

